\v 13 He's¦145109 \add ≈the¦145116 one who'll build¦145109 a temple for¦145112 me\add*, and¦145113 I¦145113 will¦145113 \add ≈make his¦145117 descendents reign\add* forever¦145120.
\v 14 I myself will¦145123 become like a father¦145126 to him, and¦145127 he'll¦145128 become like a son¦145131 to me¦145130. When¦145133 he \add ≈disobeys, I'll¦145123 punish him like fathers punish their sons\add*.\x + \xo 7:14: \xt Psa 89:26-27; 2Cor 6:18; Heb 1:5.\x*
\v 15 \add ≈But¦145141\add* my¦145141 kindness won't¦145142 turn away from you like I turned away from Sha'ul¦145149—\add ≈the one who I removed¦145151 ahead of¦145152 you\add*.
\v 16 Your \add ≈descendants\add* and¦145154 your¦145155 kingdom¦145156 will remain forever. Your throne¦145161 will be¦145162 established¦145163 forever.’ ”\x + \xo 7:16: \xt Psa 89:36-37.\x*
\s1 David's prayer
