\v 3 Then¦145478 David¦145479 \add ≈defeated¦145478\add* Tsovah's¦145487 King¦145486 Hadadezer¦145482 (son¦145483 of Rehov¦145485) \add ≈who had tried to reestablish his authority over the¦145491 Euphrates\add* River¦145491.
\v 4 David¦145497 captured¦145496 1,700 horsemen¦145503 and twenty¦145504 thousand¦145505 men on¦145507 foot¦145507. \add *He¦145509\add* hamstrung¦145508 all¦145512 the chariot¦145514 \add horses\add* except for a hundred¦145502 of them.
