\v 2 \add ≈Now\add* there was a servant¦145776 in Sha'ul¦145775 household¦145774 named Tsiva and he¦145785 was summoned¦145779 to¦145787 David¦145784, and the¦145786 king¦145786 \add ≈asked\add* him¦145787, “Are¦145788 you¦145788 Tsiva?”
\p “\add Yes, I'm\add* your¦145791 servant,” he \add ≈replied\add*.
\p
\v 3 “Is¦145795 there¦145795 \add ≈anyone¦145797 from Sha'ul's¦145799 family who's still¦145796 alive\add*?” the¦145798 king¦145794 \add ≈asked\add*. “\add If so,\add* I'd \add ≈like to show God's¦145803 kindness to them\add*.”\x + \xo 9:3: \xt 2Sam 4:4.\x*
\p “\add Yes,\add* \add ≈There's¦145795 still one of Yonatan's¦145811 sons alive\add*,” Tsiva¦145805 told the king. “\add ≈He's crippled in both¦145813 legs\add*.”
