\p
\v 23 Two¦148036 years¦148036 passed, then Abshalom's¦148040 shearers¦148039 were¦148038 in¦148041 Baal¦148041-Hatsor (near¦148044 Efrayim¦148046) and¦148047 Abshalom \add ≈invited\add* all¦148049 the¦148051 king's¦148052 sons¦148051.
\v 24 Abshalom¦148055 went¦148054 to¦148056 the king and \add ≈asked\add* him¦148065, “Listen¦148060, please¦148062, \add ≈the shearers¦148063 are working for\add* your servant. Please¦148067, let¦148065 the king and his¦148069 servants¦148069 come with¦148070 your servant.”
\p
\v 25 “No, my son¦148081,” the king¦148075 \add ≈replied\add*. “\add ≈There's too many of¦148081 us—it would be¦148088 too expensive\add* for you¦148089.” \add @Abshalom¦148078\add* he urged¦148090 him, but¦148074 he wouldn't go¦148096, \add ≈however\add* he did bless¦148097 him.
