\v 26 “But¦148099 if \add you don't come\add*,” Abshalom¦148100 \add ≈insisted\add*, “please¦148104 let¦148102 my¦148107 brother¦148107 Amnon¦148106 come with¦148105 us¦148105.”
\p “Why should¦148102 \em he\em* go¦148112 with you?” the king¦148110 \add ≈asked\add*.
\v 27 \add ≈But¦148115\add* Abshalom¦148118 \add ≈insisted, so\add* \add @the king¦148128\add* \add agreed to\add* send¦148119 Amnon¦148123 and¦148115 \add *his\add* other sons¦148127.
\v 28 Then¦148132 Abshalom¦148132 \add ≈prepared\add* his¦148135 young men, “Listen now, when Amnon \add ≈gets a bit drunk from\add* the wine¦148143 and I tell you all, ‘Strike¦148146 Amnon!’ then you'll kill¦148150 him. You all don't¦148152 \add need to\add* be¦148154 afraid¦148154 \add because\add* I myself am¦148155 the one commanding¦148158 you. Be¦148160 courageous \add ≈warriors\add*.”
\v 29 \add At the right time,\add* Abshalom's¦148168 servants¦148167 did¦148166 to¦148169 Amnon¦148169 what Abshalom commanded¦148171 \add <them\add*. All¦148175 the rest of¦148177 the king's¦148178 sons¦148177 \add ≈jumped\add* up and onto their mules and fled¦148184 \add away\add*.
\p
\v 30 \add ≈While¦148197 they¦148187 were still on¦148188 the way¦148188\add*, David¦148193 heard the news¦148189 that Abshalom¦148196 had¦148195 struck¦148195 all of his sons¦148201 and killed them¦148206, and none were left¦148205 alive.
\v 31 The king¦148211 \add ≈stood¦148221\add* up and¦148212 tore¦148212 his clothes, then he¦148216 laid¦148216 down¦148216 on the¦148217 ground¦148217. \add Meanwhile\add*, all¦148218 his servants¦148220 \add there\add* were¦148221 tearing their clothes.
\v 32 Then Yonadab¦148227 (David's¦148234 brother¦148232 Shimeah's¦148231 son¦148229) \add ≈spoke¦148226 up\add*, “My¦148239 master¦148239, don't¦148236 \add ≈imagine that\add* all¦148241 those young¦148243 men¦148243, the¦148244 king's¦148246 sons¦148244, have¦148247 been murdered¦148247. \add I suspect that\add* only Amnon¦148250 is dead, because¦148248 Abshalom¦148258 \add ≈has been determined¦148260 to do this ever since\add* his¦148265 sister¦148265 Tamar¦148264 was humiliated.
\v 33 \add ≈So¦148267 my¦148271 master¦148271, don't¦148268 believe the¦148272 report that all¦148278 your\add* sons¦148280 are dead. \add ≈It's¦148288 probably\add* only Amnon¦148287 who's dead.
\p
\v 34 \add Meanwhile,\add* Abshalom¦148293 had fled¦148292.
\p \add Suddenly\add* the watchman¦148296 \add ≈turned\add* and saw¦148301, wow, many people¦148303 coming¦148306 around the hill¦148310 along the road¦148307 behind¦148308 him¦148308.
\v 35 “Look,” Yonadab¦148313 told the king. “The king's¦148320 sons¦148318 are coming¦148321! \add ≈It's¦148325 just what I said¦148312\add*.”
\v 36 He'd¦148331 \add hardly\add* finished¦148329 speaking¦148330 when, wow, the king's¦148334 sons¦148332 came¦148335 in. Then¦148327 they all cried loudly, and the king and his¦148344 servants¦148344 \add ≈joined them in their¦148337 wailing\add*.
