\v 32 “Listen, I \add ≈tried to contact\add* you,” Abshalom¦149083 \add ≈replied\add*. “I asked you to come¦149092 here so¦149094 that¦149094 I could¦149094 send¦149094 you to the king \add ≈to ask what¦149101 the point was¦149104 of bringing me here from Geshur¦149103\add* \add if I can't see him\add*—\add ≈I might as well have¦149102 stayed back\add* there¦149109. \add ≈So¦149082\add* now¦149110, \add ≈help me to get invited to see\add* the king, and¦149082 then if \add ≈I'm considered guilty of a crime\add*, then let¦149111 him kill¦149120 me.”
\p
\v 33 \add ≈So¦149122\add* Yoav¦149123 went¦149134 and informed the king, and he called¦149130 for Abshalom¦149133. \add ≈When¦149148 he entered\add*, he \add ≈knelt and bowed¦149138 his face\add* to¦149144 the ground \add ≈in¦149144 front¦149144 of¦149144\add* the king, and then¦149122 the king kissed¦149146 \add *him\add*.
