\v 17 \add ≈So¦149471\add* the king¦149472 departed with¦149476 all¦149473 his¦149476 people¦149475, and¦149471 they¦149477 stopped¦149477 at¦149476 the last house¦149478.
\v 18 Then¦149481 all¦149481 his servants¦149483 passed¦149484 beside him to go ahead, along with¦149504 his bodyguards (the Kerethites¦149490 and the Felethites) and six hundred¦149499 Gittites (from¦149505 Gat).
\v 19 Then¦149512 the king said¦149512 to Ittai¦149516 the Gittite¦149517, “\add ≈You don't have to come\add* with us¦149523. You're a foreigner¦149531 and an exile¦149535 from your¦149537 place¦149537, \add ≈so you could\add* go¦149519 back and stay with the \add new\add* king.
\v 20 \add ≈You haven't been here long\add*, and we don't even know where¦149550 we're going. \add ≈I¦149543 certainly need to leave but¦149542 you can return¦149554 with your relatives\add*. \add May Yahweh show\add* kindness and faithfulness¦149561 \add to you all\add*.”
