\v 30 \add ≈As\add* David¦149758 was going¦149759 up¦149759 the Mt¦149760. of¦149760 Olives¦149761, he was walking¦149769 barefoot¦149770 with his head¦149765 covered. He¦149768 was weeping as were the people¦149773 with him—they \add too\add* had their heads covered and¦149758 were weeping.
\v 31 David¦149784 \add ≈knew\add* that Ahitofel was among¦149788 the people conspiring¦149788 with¦149788 Abshalom¦149791, \add ≈so\add* \add *he\add* \add ≈prayed\add*, “Please¦149796, Yahweh¦149801, make¦149794 Ahitofel \add ≈give foolish¦149794 advice\add*.”
