\v 34 \add ≈but\add* if¦149835 you return¦149838 to the city¦149837 and¦149835 tell Abshalom¦149840, ‘I'm your servant, \add ≈my\add* king¦149844. I was your father's¦149847 servant \add ≈in the past, but\add* now¦149850 I'll¦149845 be your servant,’ then¦149835 you'll¦149838 \add be able to oppose\add* Ahitofel's¦149857 counsel¦149856 for me¦149854.
