\p
\v 1 David¦149906 \add ≈hadn't gone far past the summit¦149909 when\add*, wow, he was meet¦149916 by Mefiboshet's servant¦149912 Tsiva¦149911 with a pair¦149917 of saddled¦149919 donkeys¦149918 \add ≈loaded with\add* two¦149921 hundred bread¦149922 rolls, one hundred \add ≈cakes\add* of raisins¦149924, one hundred \add pieces\add* of fresh fruit¦149926, and¦149906 a \add ≈leather container\add* of wine.\x + \xo 16:1: \xt 2Sam 9:9-10.\x*
\v 2 “\add ≈What's¦149935 all that\add*?” the¦149946 king¦149931 \add ≈asked\add*.
\p “The¦149941 donkeys¦149941 are for the king's¦149944 \add ≈family\add* to ride¦149945,” Tsiva¦149934 \add ≈answered\add*, “and the bread and fruits¦149948 are for the young¦149950 men¦149950 to eat¦149949, and the wine¦149951 is¦149952 for the people to drink¦149952 who \add ≈feel\add* faint¦149953 in¦149954 the wilderness¦149954.”
\p
\v 3 “\add ≈So¦149956\add* where's¦149958 your¦149961 master's¦149961 grandson \add Mefiboshet\add*?” \add ≈asked\add* the king.\x + \xo 16:3: \xt 2Sam 19:25-27.\x*
\p \add ≈Ha\add*, he stayed in¦149969 Yerushalem¦149969 because¦149970 he thought that \add ≈the Israelis¦149976 might give back control of his grandfather's kingdom\add*,” Tsiva¦149963 \add ≈lied\add*.
