\v 40 Then the king crossed over to Gilgal, and Kimham crossed over with him¦152703. All¦152692 the people of Yehudah brought the king over and also \add about\add* half of the people of Yisrael.
\rem /s1 An Argument over the King
\v 41 Then, wow, all the men of Yisrael¦152727 went to the king and \add ≈demanded\add*, “Why did our \add ≈relatives\add* from Yehudah¦152718 \add ≈secret\add* you away \add without inviting us\add*? They \add ≈took you and your household\add* over the Yordan, and all \add &your\add* men \add ≈as well\add*.”
\p
\v 42 All the men of Yehudah¦152747 answered the men of Yisrael¦152734, “Because the king is \add from our tribe\add*—\add ≈our close relative\add*. \add ≈Why¦152743 should that make you all angry\add*? \add ≈Do you all think that the king has rewarded us with¦152762 fancy food or other privileges\add*?”
\p
\v 43 The men of Yisrael¦152774 answered¦152766 the men of Yehudah¦152770, “\add Our ten tribes\add* \add ≈give us ten shares\add* in the king—more than you. \add ≈So\add* why \add ≈do you look down on us\add*? \add ≈Weren't we¦152789 the first to talk about¦152767 bringing our\add* king back \add to Yerushalem\add*?”
\p \add ≈But¦152766\add* \add ≈what the men of Yehudah said\add* was harsher than \add ≈what the ten other tribes said\add*.
