\v 2 \add ≈So¦152872\add* all the men of Yisrael¦152876 \add ≈left\add* David¦152878 \add ≈and went with\add* Sheva¦152880 (Bikri's sons), but¦152872 the men of Judah \add ≈stayed with\add* their¦152887 king¦152887 from¦152888 the Yordan¦152890 river and uphill to Yerushalem¦152893.
\p
\v 3 \add ≈When¦152895\add* David¦152896 \add ≈got back\add* to his¦152899 Yerushalem¦152900 \add ≈palace\add*, the ten¦152904 slave-wives that he'd \add ≈left¦152910 behind\add* to guard¦152911 the \add ≈palace\add*, \add *he\add* \add ≈moved\add* them into a \add separate house\add*. \add That place was\add* guarded and¦152895 he provided¦152917 for them, but¦152895 he didn't¦152919 \add ≈sleep with\add* them—\add ≈thus\add* they were¦152922 locked¦152923 up¦152923 until¦152924 \add ≈they died¦152927 living¦152929 as widows¦152928\add*.\x + \xo 20:3: \xt 2Sam 16:22.\x*
\p
\v 4 \add One day\add* the king¦152933 told Amasa¦152936 \add (his new army commander)\add*, “Summon¦152937 the men of Yehudah¦152944 to \add ≈be here in three¦152945 days¦152946, and you be with them\add*.”
