\v 6 \add Meanwhile\add* David¦152967 told Abishai¦152970, “Bikri's son¦152975 Sheva¦152974 will¦152972 do more harm to us now¦152971 than¦152978 Abshalom¦152980. Take¦152982 \add ≈some of my warriors\add* and \add ≈chase him¦152988 down\add*, in case he¦152991 finds¦152991 \add ≈some fortified¦152994 city to hide in and gets away from us\add*.”
\v 7 \add ≈So¦152998 Yoav's¦153001 men¦153000 and the king's bodyguards\add* and all¦153004 the \add ≈best warriors¦153000\add* left Yerushalem¦153008 to¦153009 \add ≈hunt Sheba¦153011 down\add*.
\v 8 \add ≈When they were¦153017 approaching\add* the huge¦153020 rock¦153019 at¦153022 Gibeon¦153022, they met Amasa¦153023. Yoav¦153026 was¦153027 \add ≈dressed for battle with¦153022 a dagger strapped to his waist¦153038 under his robe\add*. \add ≈As he stepped forward¦153041, he allowed his sword¦153034 to drop to the ground\add* \add from his hand\add*.
