\v 21 \add ≈That's not¦153286 what we're here for\add*. \add We're here\add* for a man¦153291 from the Efrayim¦153293 hills named Sheva¦153294, the son¦153295 of¦153295 Bikri. He¦153299 \add ≈took a stand\add* against the king¦153301—against David¦153302. \add Just\add* \add ≈hand¦153300 him over to us, and¦153307 then we'll leave your\add* city¦153309.”
\p “\add ≈Wait\add*,” the woman¦153311 told Yoav¦153314. “His¦153316 head¦153316 will be¦153317 thrown¦153317 over the wall¦153320 to you¦153318.”
\v 22 \add ≈So¦153322\add* the woman¦153323 went to all¦153326 the people¦153328 \add ≈with¦153329\add* her¦153329 wisdom¦153329, and they¦153330 \add ≈decapitated\add* Sheva¦153334, and threw¦153338 \add @his head¦153333\add* \add down\add* to Yoav. Then¦153322 he¦153342 \add ≈signalled\add* on¦153329 the trumpet¦153343, and \add @his men\add* \add ≈left the area and went back to their homes\add*, and Yoav returned¦153351 to the king¦153355 at¦153329 Yerushalem¦153352.
